        owl:deprecated         "false";
        owl:versionInfo        "1";
        skos:altLabel          "";
        skos:definition        "\"Exploring the climate history and the geological structure and evolution of the rocks and mountains of Antarctica\uFFFDs continental interior provides clues to past, present and future environmental change. Under-ice lakes, mountain chains buried by up to 4km ice, and sea bed sediments surrounding the frozen continent provide an unparalleled record of how the Earth\uFFFDs climate has changed over millions of years.\""@en;
